# TASK-059 — Board artwork and attached presentation

Priority: P2
Requirements: REQ-006, REQ-021, REQ-022, REQ-023 (`REQ-23-misc`)

## Request

We currently have very basic drawn assets for the towns and cities, and
plain colour for the tile background. Additionally, there is a slight separation of the assets and background when zooming.

I want custom-created picture assets for these, made using whatever approach you deem most appropriate. I want them to look cartoonish and professional.

Also, please, once again, make sure that the arrow atop the stats bar stays connected to the bar at all times, and moves with it.
Also, the yellow crown showing who has the longest road should be a circle surrounding that number rather than next to it.

## Accepted plan

User approved the implementation plan with the following addition: terrain artwork must be minimal, cohesive, and quiet. Provide one code opacity setting tagged `// # terrainalpha`, fading artwork into each terrain's existing plain colour.

1. Generate seven restrained terrain illustrations and settlement/city artwork; integrate project-owned assets with legible tokens, owner colours, and outlined white building tiles.
2. Use one board transform for zoom, keeping terrain, pieces, and hit targets aligned.
3. Attach the stats arrow/tab/table to one moving surface.
4. Surround the centred Longest Road number with a gold ring, preserving tied-player drag reassignment.
5. Add focused regression coverage, review the diff, run available checks, and record manual acceptance needs.

