## Implementation and validation

- `BoardArtwork.swift` centralises the asset names and `terrainOpacity = 0.45 // # terrainalpha`. Zero restores the exact existing plain-colour tile; one shows the complete image. The setting affects only terrain artwork, preserving token and piece contrast.
- The built-in image_gen tool generated nine project-owned PNGs: seven `Terrain-<terrain>.imageset` images and `Building-settlement.imageset` / `Building-city.imageset` under `HexIQ/Assets.xcassets/`. Original outputs are copied unchanged, including building alpha. No dependency was added. Full prompts: [artwork generation notes](TASK-059-artwork-prompts.md).
- Hexes, roads, real/ghost buildings, vertex values, and editing targets use fixed unzoomed geometry, with one enclosing scale/offset. The named picker coordinate space lives inside that transform; the pan coordinate space stays outside it. Tap-to-centre accounts for the displayed board rotation.
- Building images multiply their neutral surfaces by the player colour, preserving black linework, and retain white outlined tiles. Tokens and buildings still counter-rotate to remain upright.
- The stats drawer uses one continuous tab/table background, an explicit table accessibility container, and a vector chevron. One translation moves the full surface; there are no separate tab/table backgrounds to diverge.
- A 30-point gold stroke surrounds the independently centred road number. The existing 0.5-second hold/drag and tied-player domain rules remain in place; the moving cell has elevated stacking order.

